1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,344
Who Turned Off the Wi-Fi?

3
00:00:03,344 --> 00:00:06,937
Emma and I are on a video call, planning our class poster.

4
00:00:06,937 --> 00:00:10,937
She holds up a sketch, opens her mouth, and turns into a statue.

5
00:00:10,937 --> 00:00:12,740
The screen is frozen.

6
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,823
Emma?

7
00:00:13,823 --> 00:00:15,167
Can you hear me?

8
00:00:15,436 --> 00:00:18,657
If she's doing a robot impression, it's really good.

9
00:00:18,892 --> 00:00:21,115
My phone says there's no connection.

10
00:00:21,115 --> 00:00:22,688
Is it working for you?

11
00:00:22,688 --> 00:00:25,240
Ben checks his tablet and shakes his head.

12
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:28,271
We call Dad, who is putting away the vacuum cleaner.

13
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:30,096
Let me have a look.

14
00:00:30,096 --> 00:00:31,919
Did it stop just now?

15
00:00:32,188 --> 00:00:33,734
About a minute ago.

16
00:00:33,734 --> 00:00:36,432
Dad follows the cable from the router to the wall.

17
00:00:36,432 --> 00:00:39,098
The plug is hanging loose beside the outlet.

18
00:00:39,364 --> 00:00:40,983
That would explain it.

19
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:43,733
I must have unplugged it when I moved the vacuum.

20
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:45,212
My mistake.

21
00:00:45,484 --> 00:00:47,530
So the internet wasn't broken.

22
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:49,426
It was just taking a nap.

23
00:00:49,708 --> 00:00:51,285
Something like that.

24
00:00:51,285 --> 00:00:53,056
I'll plug it back in.

25
00:00:53,056 --> 00:00:54,545
Give it a minute.

26
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,241
We wait while the little lights come back on.

27
00:00:57,241 --> 00:01:00,637
I open our call again, and Emma finally starts moving.

28
00:01:00,866 --> 00:01:01,743
There you are!

29
00:01:01,743 --> 00:01:03,045
Did you see my drawing?

30
00:01:03,316 --> 00:01:05,028
Only the first half.

31
00:01:05,028 --> 00:01:07,393
You looked very serious for a while.

32
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:09,133
That's my thinking face.

33
00:01:09,412 --> 00:01:12,760
We finish planning on paper, then take photos to share.

34
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:15,989
Dad promises to check the plugs next time he cleans.

35
00:01:15,989 --> 00:01:19,645
Ben promises to tell everyone he personally watched the internet wake up.

36
00:01:19,645 --> 00:01:22,937
Somehow, that becomes the biggest news of the afternoon.
